WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.788
Ruby2ßhell

00:00:01.907 --> 00:00:03.168
pre-authentication

00:00:02.991 --> 00:00:04.265
RCE on stock

00:00:04.076 --> 00:00:04.772
Rails

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.772
Veria Labs disclosed

00:00:06.584 --> 00:00:07.633
a heap overflow

00:00:07.444 --> 00:00:08.470
in Ruby's case

00:00:08.282 --> 00:00:09.743
conversion for single-byte

00:00:09.555 --> 00:00:10.357
encodings

00:00:10.558 --> 00:00:11.760
reachable from default

00:00:11.572 --> 00:00:12.927
Rails and Sinatra

00:00:12.739 --> 00:00:13.293
apps

00:00:13.506 --> 00:00:15.534
Ruby 3.3.14

00:00:15.687 --> 00:00:19.637
3.4.13 and 4.0.10

00:00:19.449 --> 00:00:20.203
fix it

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:21.807
The output buffer

00:00:21.618 --> 00:00:22.538
is the input

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.363
length plus 20

00:00:23.175 --> 00:00:24.660
bytes so 21

00:00:24.484 --> 00:00:26.193
ß characters overflow

00:00:26.005 --> 00:00:26.689
it by one

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:27.019
byte

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:28.379
The bug dates

00:00:28.191 --> 00:00:29.086
back to Ruby

00:00:28.898 --> 00:00:30.808
2.4.0 and is

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:31.940
reached by and

00:00:32.023 --> 00:00:33.768
UTF-8 strings are

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.511
not affected

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.569
The same loop

00:00:35.417 --> 00:00:36.300
is in several

00:00:36.112 --> 00:00:40.216
ISO-8859 and Windows-125x

00:00:40.027 --> 00:00:40.805
encodings

00:00:40.912 --> 00:00:41.619
and has been

00:00:41.431 --> 00:00:42.550
there since Ruby

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:44.083
2.4.0

00:00:44.622 --> 00:00:45.636
Full story on

00:00:45.447 --> 00:00:46.343
the dashboard
